it occupies. How it stands there away offshore, more lonely than the Eddie

6
00:00:22,959 --> 00:00:28,477
Stone Lighthouse. Look at it. A mere hillock and elbow of sand, all beach and

7
00:00:28,478 --> 00:00:32,798
without a background. There is more sand there than you would use in 20 years as

8
00:00:32,799 --> 00:00:37,519
a substitute for blotting paper. Some gamesome whites will tell you that they

9
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:41,999
have to plant weeds there, that they don't grow naturally, that they import

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,798
Canada thistles, that they have to send beyond seas for a spile to stop a leak

11
00:00:46,799 --> 00:00:51,839
in an oil cask, that pieces of wood in Nantucket are carried about like bits of

12
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:56,638
the true cross in Rome, that people there plant toad stools before their

13
00:00:56,639 --> 00:01:01,278
house to get under the shade in summertime. That one blade of grass

14
00:01:01,279 --> 00:01:06,558
makes an oasis, three blades in a day's walk a prairie. That they wear quicksand

15
00:01:06,559 --> 00:01:11,199
shoes, something like laplander snowshoes. That they are so shut up,

16
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:15,599
belted about every way enclosed, surrounded, and made an utter island of

17
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:20,878
by the ocean, that to their very chairs and tables small clams will sometimes be

18
00:01:20,879 --> 00:01:25,039
found adhering as to the backs of sea turtles.

19
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:30,638
But these extravaganzas only show that Nantucket is no Illinois.

20
00:01:30,639 --> 00:01:34,558
Look now at the wondrous traditional story of how this island was settled by

21
00:01:34,559 --> 00:01:39,919
the Red Men. Thus goes the legend. In olden times an eagle swooped down upon

22
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:44,878
the New England coast and carried off an infant Indian in its talons. With loud

23
00:01:44,879 --> 00:01:49,759
laments the parents saw their child born out of sight over the wide waters. They

24
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:53,759
resolved to follow in the same direction. Setting out in their canoes

25
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:57,839
after a perilous passage they discovered the island, and there they found an

26
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:02,878
empty ivory casket, the poor little Indians skeleton.

27
00:02:02,879 --> 00:02:06,638
What wonder then, that these Nantucketers, born on a beach, should

28
00:02:06,639 --> 00:02:11,278
take to the sea for a livelihood. They first caught crabs and quhogs in the

29
00:02:11,279 --> 00:02:16,317
sand. Grown boulder, they waited out with nets for mackerel. More experience

30
00:02:16,318 --> 00:02:21,278
they pushed off in boats and captured Cod, and at last launching a navy of

31
00:02:21,279 --> 00:02:26,317
great ships on the sea, explored this watery world, put an incessant belt of

32
00:02:26,318 --> 00:02:31,759
circumnavigations round it, peeped in at bearing straits, and in all seasons and

33
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:36,558
all oceans declared everlasting war with the mightiest animated mass that has

34
00:02:36,559 --> 00:02:41,759
survived the flood, most monstrous and most mountainous, that Himalayan salt

35
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:46,718
seam mastadon, clothed with such portentiousness, of unconscious power

36
00:02:46,719 --> 00:02:50,638
that his very panics are more to be dreaded than his most fearless and

37
00:02:50,639 --> 00:02:56,078
malicious assaults. And thus of these naked Nantucketers, these sea hermits,

38
00:02:56,079 --> 00:03:00,638
issuing from their antill in the sea, overrun and conquered the watery world

39
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:05,679
like so many Alexanders, parceling out among them the Atlantic, Pacific, and

40
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:11,199
Indian oceans, as the three pirate powers did Poland. Let America add

41
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:16,718
Mexico to Texas and pile Cuba upon Canada. Let the English overswarm all

42
00:03:16,719 --> 00:03:21,919
India and hang out their blazing banner from the sun. Twothirds of this

43
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:25,278
terraquous globe are the Nantucketers.

44
00:03:25,279 --> 00:03:30,558
For the sea is his. He owns it as emperor's own empires. Other seaman

45
00:03:30,559 --> 00:03:32,798
having but a right of way through it.

46
00:03:32,799 --> 00:03:37,519
Merchant ships are but extension bridges, armed ones but floating forts.

47
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:41,278
Even pirates and privateeers, though following the sea as highwaymen the

48
00:03:41,279 --> 00:03:45,358
road, they but plunder other ships, other fragments of the land like

49
00:03:45,359 --> 00:03:49,519
themselves, without seeking to draw their living from the bottomless deep

50
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:55,599
itself. The Nantucketer, he alone resides and riots on the sea. He alone,

51
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:01,358
in Bible language, goes down to it in ships, to and fro, plowing it as his own

52
00:04:01,359 --> 00:04:04,638
special plantation. There is his home.

53
00:04:04,639 --> 00:04:09,119
There lies his business which a Noah's flood would not interrupt, though it

54
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:11,839
overwhelmed all the millions in China.

55
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:17,119
He lives on the sea as prairie in the prairie. He hides among the waves.

56
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:22,158
He climbs them as shamwa hunters climb the Alps. For years he knows not the

57
00:04:22,159 --> 00:04:26,638
land, so that when he comes to it at last it smells like another world, more

58
00:04:26,639 --> 00:04:31,438
strangely than the moon would to an earthman. with the landless gull that at

59
00:04:31,439 --> 00:04:36,317
sunset folds her wings and is rocked to sleep between billows. So at nightfall

60
00:04:36,318 --> 00:04:42,317
the nantucketer out of sight of land furls his sails and lays him to his rest

61
00:04:42,318 --> 00:04:49,239
while under his very pillow rush herds of walruses and whales.
